 A    display an Alphabetized list of all downloadable files (or by lib).
 B    Browse file descriptions. optional ( B filename or B filenumber )
 C    Comment. (leave a private message for the Sysop)
 D    Download file menu.   optional ( D filenames and/or filenumbers )
 E    read or write or find Email. (private messages)
 F    from FILE or ALL menu: go to Filelist archiver menu.
      from MSG or MAIN menu: go to Files menu.
 FL   Edit your Friends List for fast access to Email.
 G    Goodbye. (Hangup!)
 I    read system bulletins, help files, and general Interest textfiles.
 J    Jump to the rexxdoors area. An area of ARexx diversion.
 L    select and List file library.  optional ( L lib# or lib# )
       "List 7" lists ALL files in Library 7, "7" lists NEW files only.
 M    go to the Message conferences menu.
 N    short form filelist by date or list of all New (un-browsed) files.
 O    information about the Other users of this system.
 P    Post (write) public messages.
 R    Read public messages.  optional ( R conf#  or  R A  or  R N )
 S    MAIN: Search through the userlist.
 S    MSG: Search full text of all public messages.
 S    FILE: Search file descriptions.
 T    Transfer protocol menu.
 U    Upload file.              optional ( U filename )
 V    View the simple log of the last 99 users.
 W    Who is here. the email address (name) of all users.
 X    eXpert. toggles menus on and off.
 Y    view/edit Your user parameters and information.
 Z    show bbs and user statistics, unread messages, etc.
 !    Try to get the Sysop's attention for a chat.
 $    toggles between 3 small menus or one large menu.
 #    toggles color on and off.
 +    select files to download from extra (not BBS libs) devices.
 ,    display graph of average minutes of use per hour.
 .    (period) go to the main menu.
OFF   logs off without asking for comment to sysop.
BYE   same as OFF
QUICK offline archiver options.

CTRL-E aborts most commands that are in progress.
Attempts to use CTRL-C with this BBS software may cause a disconnect.
